---
// A label above the first role that is not on the resume. Hidden until the page is opened through the
// resume link (see revealEarlier in TimelineList.astro). It runs from the left edge of the logos to the
// right edge of the dates and locations, so it lines up with the row content and not with the highlight.
// It shows with data-show, or from the first paint when the section is open through its anchor link (see
// data-open in TimelineList.astro). The display rules live here and not in Tailwind classes, because
// Tailwind's own `[hidden]` rule is a layered !important that no plain rule can beat.
---

<li data-earlier-divider class="items-center gap-3 pb-5 text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
  <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-gray-200 dark:bg-neutral-700" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span>Not on the resume</span>
  <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-gray-200 dark:bg-neutral-700" aria-hidden="true"></span>
</li>

<style is:global>
  [data-earlier-divider] {
    display: none;
  }

  [data-earlier-divider][data-show],
  section[data-open]:not([data-ready]) [data-earlier-divider] {
    display: flex;
  }
</style>
